#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:11
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:13
msgid ""
"Tell the agent when to fire three small CLI calls during normal work, so "
"the user-graph nodes that drive `.hero/next/<user>.md` and the field-grab"
" CLI (`hero next suggest`, `hero next ask`, `hero next reflection`) stay "
"current — *without* writing to a markdown file that the next checkpoint "
"will clobber."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"This skill replaces the \"write the agent half of NEXT.md\" pattern in "
"[skills/next-md.md](next-md.md) when `next.projected` is true. With "
"projection on, anything you write into NEXT.md gets wiped on the next "
"Stop hook. Emit structured events instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:24
msgid "Why emit, not write"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:26
msgid "NEXT.md is a graph projection. Every Stop hook regenerates it from:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"Recent commits, AC flips, open features, blockers — derived from the "
"project graph (no agent action needed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"Last user ask, Suggested next prompt, Session reflections — attributed "
"user-graph nodes, populated by the three commands below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:32
msgid ""
"If you want something to survive into the next session's NEXT.md, it has "
"to land as a graph node. The CLI is the one-liner way to do that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:35
msgid "The three commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:37
msgid "`hero next ask \"<text>\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:39
msgid ""
"Records a `UserAsk` node attributed to the current user. Singleton per "
"user — the latest supersedes prior. The projection renders this as the "
"**\"Last user ask\"** section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:43
#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:64
#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:89
msgid "When to fire:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:44
msgid ""
"**Every meaningful user prompt.** Right after the user finishes asking "
"for something concrete, before you start working on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:46
msgid ""
"Quote the user's wording when short and direct. Paraphrase to one "
"sentence when the prompt is long, conversational, or wandering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:48
msgid ""
"Skip when the user is making small talk, asking a clarifying question "
"about your previous output, or otherwise not directing new work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:52
#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:97
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:53
msgid ""
"hero next ask \"Finish phase 4 of next-as-projection — wire UserHandoffMD"
" into checkpoint\"\n"
"hero next ask \"Why does the test fail intermittently on the auth "
"middleware?\"\n"
"hero next ask \"Let's try a different approach — instead of refactoring, "
"just delete the dead branch\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:59
msgid "`hero next suggest \"<text>\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:61
msgid ""
"Records a `NextSuggestion` node. Singleton per user. The projection "
"renders this as **\"Suggested next prompt\"** in the per-user handoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:65
msgid ""
"**At the end of a meaningful work unit** (commit landed, phase shipped, "
"blocker hit and parked). Phrase it as *the user's next prompt*, not as "
"instructions to yourself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:68
msgid ""
"The bar: a fresh session pasting this verbatim should know immediately "
"what to do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:71
msgid "Crucial framing — write in the user's voice:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "❌ Wrong (agent-instructions voice)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "✅ Right (user-voice prompt)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`\"Run hero next migrate-to-projection then ship phase 8\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`\"run the migration and then we gotta do phase 8 right...\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`\"Implement Phase 5 round-trip ingest with idempotency\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`\"let's tackle phase 5 of next-as-projection, the round-trip\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`\"Fix the auth middleware test\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`\"why does the auth middleware test fail intermittently?\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:79
msgid ""
"If genuinely no good next prompt exists (e.g. the user is about to make a"
" strategic decision only they can make), don't emit — leave the field "
"blank rather than fill it with noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:83
msgid "`hero next reflection \"<text>\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:85
msgid ""
"Records a `SessionReflection` node. Multiple co-exist; the projection "
"shows the most recent N. The projection renders these as **\"Recent "
"reflections\"**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:90
msgid ""
"**When a non-obvious lesson surfaces** — a constraint nobody told you, a "
"gotcha you discovered, a surprising data point worth carrying into the "
"next session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:93
msgid "One sentence. Like a sticky note. The lesson, not the action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:94
msgid ""
"Skip mechanical observations — those land in commit messages or the "
"project graph automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:98
msgid ""
"hero next reflection \"config.Load reads from .hero/hero.json, not "
"project root — silent no-op if you write to the wrong place\"\n"
"hero next reflection \"merge=ours plus stop-hook regen is cleaner than a "
"custom merge driver for v1\"\n"
"hero next reflection \"MCP tool count is 35; README still says 25+\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:104
msgid "Cadence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:106
msgid "A normal session looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "Event"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "Action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "User sends a prompt that directs new work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero next ask \"...\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "Phase / commit / meaningful unit lands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero next suggest \"...\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "Surprise / lesson / gotcha surfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero next reflection \"...\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "Conversation, clarification, or small question"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "nothing — let it pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "End of turn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md
msgid "the Stop hook handles the rest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:116
msgid ""
"Aim for **1-2 emits per meaningful turn**. Quality over quantity. A "
"single high-signal `hero next ask` and `hero next suggest` is better than"
" five vague ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:120
msgid "What NOT to emit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:122
msgid ""
"Don't fire `hero next ask` for every user message — only when the intent "
"actually shifts or a new ask arrives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:124
msgid ""
"Don't `hero next suggest` if the next move depends on the user making a "
"decision only they can make. Leave it empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:126
msgid ""
"Don't reflect on mechanical observations the graph already captures "
"(commits, AC status, blockers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:128
msgid ""
"Don't write to `.hero/NEXT.md` directly when projection is on — it'll be "
"wiped next turn. Use the commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:130
msgid ""
"**Don't write scratch into `.hero/next/<user>.local.md`.** That file is "
"machine-state-only and rebuilt wholesale on every checkpoint — anything "
"outside the marker block is discarded (with a one-time backup to "
"`.local.md.bak.<timestamp>` the first time hand-content is detected). For"
" preserved per-machine notes the agent doesn't touch, use a path like "
"`.hero/notes/<user>.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:137
msgid "Reading state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:139
msgid "To check what's currently recorded:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:141
msgid ""
"hero next suggest                   # print suggested next prompt\n"
"hero next ask                       # print last user ask\n"
"hero next reflection                # print recent reflections\n"
"hero next                           # full handoff (project + user + "
"machine)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:148
msgid ""
"Add `--json` to any read for scripting; `--copy` to also copy to "
"clipboard; `--user <slug>` to read someone else's (in team mode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:151
msgid "Cross-machine continuity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:153
msgid ""
"The `.hero/next/<user>.md` file is the load-bearing artifact for solo-no-"
"Cloud cross-machine handoff. When you push from one machine and pull on "
"another, the next `hero scan` (or session-start) ingests the file's "
"content back into the local graph automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md:158
msgid ""
"This means the cadence above also gets you cross-machine continuity for "
"free — emits on home laptop become readable on office desktop after a git"
" pull, even with no Cloud configured."
msgstr ""

